  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Statement I : Sodium hydride can be used as an oxidising agent.</p><p>Statement II : The lone pair of electrons on nitrogen in pyridine makes it basic.</p><p>Choose the CORRECT answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NPihh",
      "text": "Both statement I and statement II are false",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Xw0s5",
      "text": "Statement I is true but statement II is false",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "PuFv1",
      "text": "Statement I is false but statement II is true",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zX54D",
      "text": "Both statement I and statement II are true",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(1)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaH</mi></math> (sodium Hydride) is used as a reducing reagent.</p><p>(2)&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/62544822-457a-49cb-ad07-c65cfa1376f2-image.png\" style=\"width: 62px; height: 75px;\" /> In pyridine, due to free electron on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> atom, it is basic in nature.</p><p>Hence, statement I is false and II is true.</p>",
    "image": null
